# TASK-05 evaluation

Run from `/home/hong/SLAM`:

```bash
source env.sh
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 /home/hong/SLAM/.venv/bin/python -m tools.eval.run_all_eval
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 /home/hong/SLAM/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tools/tests -q
```

Every product, including `gt_gnss_enu_tum.txt`, is under `results/eval/`.
This resolves TASKS.md's GT-path example in favor of its explicit output-only
restriction. Source bags, experiment directories and TASK-06 trees are untouched.
Individual CLIs use `python -m tools.eval.gnss_gt`, `traj_eval`,
`build_map_from_poses` and `map_quality`; see `--help`.

`build_map_from_poses` accepts all/even/odd zero-based scan indices. SLERP
interpolates rotations and linear interpolation translates scan headers;
there is no point deskew or pose extrapolation. NPZ stores xyz,
relative_time_s, stamp_s and count. Times are weighted voxel means, allowing
provenance through downsampling rather than pretending each voxel is an
original return. Overlap caches retain those fields for first/last windows.
Voxel merges are incremental and enforce a 3-million-voxel limit.

MME is differential Gaussian entropy in nats (negative values are valid).
MPV is the smallest sample-covariance eigenvalue in m². Both use radius
0.3 m, min 6 neighbors, floor 1e-9 m², all eligible 0.1 m voxel points.
Saved GlobalMap points are transformed into ENU before voxelization and
cropped to the same GNSS XY bounding box, with height unconstrained.
Coverage and eligible-neighbor fractions accompany each value.

Overlap NN statistics concatenate both directions, restricting each to
points within 1 m of the other cloud. The >0.2 m fraction is a discrepancy
proxy that includes different visibility and sampling, not a detector of
semantic double walls. Acquisition windows are the first/last 15 s of GNSS
time, intersected with final pose support.

RPE uses every matched start and the first end at or beyond each requested
GT distance, with actual distance as denominator. GNSS yaw comes from a 2 m
centered position tangent, roll/pitch zero. It includes antenna/body-origin
and body-heading effects and is an approximation, particularly at corners.

The default GNSS filter uses status >=2 and horizontal sigma <=0.05 m on
cov[0]/cov[4]. Vertical sigma is reported without the 5 cm cutoff.
Horizontal (2D) ATE after SE3 alignment is primary; 3D ATE is retained.

`loop_validation.csv` evaluates v3 recorded marker pairs. The latest cumulative
`loop_edges` LINE_LIST records current/previous endpoint coordinates, marker time,
wall and simulation receive times; snapshots retain earlier observations. After
saving the final keyframes, endpoints are matched independently to nearest final
poses. Evaluation rejects matches over 0.2 m. GT is interpolated at the paired
keyframe stamps; horizontal distance <2 m is TRUE_POSITIVE, otherwise FALSE_POSITIVE.
The proximity criterion does not independently test rotational consistency.
Final versus online ATE does not isolate a single loop insertion.

The first line of summary.md gives the median loop ON final 2D SE3+lever ATE run
for TASK-06. Each run has align_se3.json with R, t and a homogeneous 4x4
transform from LIO-SAM odom to first-fix GNSS ENU; it uses the standard SE3 fit.

Joint lever estimation uses unbounded ordinary least squares over global
rotation, translation, and a 3D body-frame lever. Planar motion weakly
observes its vertical component; singular values and condition number are
recorded. Treat its improved in-sample ATE as diagnostic, not independent
validation of an estimated antenna offset. `|l| > 3 m` is flagged.
# Held-out fixed-map localization

From `/home/hong/SLAM`:

```bash
source env.sh
PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 \
  .venv/bin/python -m tools.loc.run_loc_eval --resume
PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 \
  .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q
PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 \
  .venv/bin/python -m tools.loc.verify_loc
```

`run_loc_eval --help` exposes map run/bag, scan parity, query bag, GNSS GT,
initial pose and query-time map reference arguments. `--map-bag` defaults to the
full original preprocessed bag, and **only even indices** are used in the prior.
For an already-even bag, select `--map-scan-filter all` to avoid splitting twice.
All outputs are constrained to `results/loc/` (including child experiment dirs).
Use a separate `--out results/loc/<experiment>` for different inputs; resume
rejects changed configuration, trajectory/GT hashes or implementation hashes.

Default: 1089 odd scans, range 1–80 m, voxel 0.3 m, fixed 0.2 m prior,
20-neighbor planar GICP covariances, epsilon 0.001, 1.0/0.5 m correspondence
gates, 30 iterations per stage. No IMU/GNSS or ongoing map poses enter tracking.
Mapping poses initialize the baseline and each robustness trial only. The first
map pose is later than the first scan; this explicit endpoint hold is disclosed
in the summary. Interpolation for robustness references never extrapolates.

`localize.py` provides the reusable registration, predictor, failure state and
streaming tracker. Its standalone CLI consumes a prior NPZ plus initial TUM.
`run_loc_eval.py` produces the baseline, paired-seed 200-trial benchmark,
GNSS metrics and plots. Trial JSON checkpoints are retained for inspection.
`verify_loc.py` independently audits the default experiment, parity separation,
input file preservation, trajectory coverage, thresholds and all trial cells,
and compares cached GICP with the public Open3D API on three real scans.

Open3D's public `registration_generalized_icp` rebuilds the target search tree
on every invocation and does not expose iterations. The cached outer loop uses
its actual `TransformationEstimationForGeneralizedICP.compute_transformation`
solver with the same convergence criteria and planar covariance model, using
one persistent scipy cKDTree. Unit tests and the real-scan audit compare it with
the public API. This is an explicit API adaptation to meet fixed-tree caching
and actual iteration accounting; it is not a different registration solver.
Reference: [Open3D implementation](https://github.com/isl-org/Open3D/blob/main/cpp/open3d/pipelines/registration/GeneralizedICP.cpp).

The two ATE variants use the unchanged TASK-05 `evaluate()` function. In
addition to the requested keyframe baseline, a common-timestamp comparison
avoids differences caused by keyframe versus dense-scan sampling. The primary
lever2D fit remains an in-sample nuisance estimate, and the same-journey split
is an optimistic estimate of true revisit performance.

`PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1` is necessary here because the user site contains numpy 2.x
and a conflicting matplotlib. Dependencies installed for this task are confined
to `.venv`; the recorded environment is `results/loc/venv_packages.txt`.
The project `pytest.ini` limits discovery to `tools/`; vendored GTSAM/pybind11
source tests need their own build environments and are not project tests.

For a different-day revisit, `--initial-pose X Y Z QX QY QZ QW` supplies the
known initial map-frame pose; `--reference-traj` supplies query-time map-frame
poses for the 200-trial convergence reference. In that mode, the table and
`mapping_baseline/` metrics refer to this supplied query reference. An independent
query-time reference is necessary to score map-frame robustness on a new bag.
For GNSS-only revisit evaluation without that reference, reuse the streaming
tracker and evaluate its output separately:

```bash
# initial_map_frame_tum.txt: >=3 valid TUM rows covering the query start time;
# only its interpolated pose at the first scan initializes tracking.
PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 \
  .venv/bin/python -m tools.loc.localize \
  --prior results/loc/prior_map.npz --query-bag path/to/revisit_bag \
  --initial-traj initial_map_frame_tum.txt --out results/loc/revisit
PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 .venv/bin/python -m tools.eval.traj_eval \
  --traj results/loc/revisit/loc_traj_tum.txt --gt query_gnss_tum.txt \
  --out results/loc/revisit/eval
```
# TASK-06 rev1 지도 내보내기

프로젝트 루트에서 `.venv` Python과 `env.sh`를 사용한다. 입력 bag과 run은
읽기 전용이며 출력은 `results/maps/<run>/`이다.

```bash
source env.sh
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2 \
  .venv/bin/python tools/maps/export_maps.py --run loop_on_r2 \
  --align-json results/eval/loop_on_r2/align_se3.json --compare-stride10
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2 \
  .venv/bin/python tools/maps/verify_maps.py results/maps/loop_on_r2
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q \
  tools/tests tools/maps/test_revision.py -k 'not spec_threshold_conflict' \
  -o cache_dir=results/maps/.pytest_cache
```

기본값은 `--scan-stride 2`, 여백 30 m, 해상도 0.05 m이다.
`--compare-stride10`은 같은 v3 입력/알고리즘으로 stride 10 기준값도 계산한다.
`--run`, `--bag`으로 입력을 바꿀 수 있다. even run은 `data/lio_bag_even`을 쓴다.
모든 설정과 입력 SHA256, 렌더러 결과, 주행 영역 통계는 `map2d_stats.json`에 남는다.

| 산출물 | 내용 |
|---|---|
| map_full.pcd | intensity를 포함한 원본 바이트 복사 |
| map_0p10.pcd | 전체 0.1 m voxel XYZ centroid, intensity 제외 |
| map_crop.pcd | 궤적 bounding box +30 m 영역의 원본 crop |
| map_crop_0p10.pcd | 동일 영역의 0.1 m voxel crop |
| map_0p10_enu.pcd, map_crop_0p10_enu.pcd | SE3 정렬을 적용한 전체/crop voxel 지도 |
| map2d.pgm, map2d.yaml | Nav2 trinary 지도, 유일한 YAML |
| map_top.png, map_oblique.png, map2d.png | crop 영역 높이/사선/occupancy 뷰 및 궤적 |
| map_loop_overlap.png | loop_on_r2 / loop_off_r2 공통 ENU 영역 확대 비교 |

정렬 JSON은 `R`(3x3), `t`(3,)를 포함한다. `p_enu = R @ p_map + t`이고
스케일이나 lever arm은 적용하지 않는다. 정렬 파일이 없으면 선택 ENU PCD는
생략하고 이유를 기록한다. 기본 PCD와 2D 지도, top/oblique는 map frame이다.
ON/OFF 비교 그림은 각각의 `results/eval/<run>/align_se3.json`을 읽어 ENU로 맞춘다.
대표 run의 비교 그림에는 loop_off_r2 입력과 정렬 파일도 필요하다.

지면은 2 m XY 셀별 하위 10 percentile이다. 빈 셀은 최근접 관측 셀을 사용한다.
장애물은 지면 위 0.3–2.0 m이다. bag 원본 스캔에 최종 keyframe 선형/SLERP
보간 자세를 적용하고, 동일 높이 슬라이스에서 0.5도 방위각별 최근접 점을
레이 끝점으로 쓴다. 수평거리 60 m 이내의 레이로 log-odds를 갱신하며, 전역
장애물 prior에 닿으면 중단한다. 포인트별 deskew는 적용하지 않는다.
미관측/불확실 셀은 unknown이며, 지면 추정 오차·가림·수평 슬라이스의 한계가 있다.

PGM은 P5, occupied=0 / free=254 / unknown=205이다. 첫 행은 지도 위쪽,
YAML origin은 왼쪽 아래 모서리이다. `occupied_thresh=0.65`,
`free_thresh=0.196`으로 gray 205가 unknown을 유지한다
(`1-205/255 = 0.196078`). 보조 YAML은 생성하지 않는다.

Open3D OffscreenRenderer를 별도 프로세스에서 먼저 시도하고, 실패하면 matplotlib
3D scatter로 대체한다. 렌더 voxel은 0.2 m, matplotlib 점 수는 최대 16만이다.
주행 영역 unknown 비율은 궤적 polyline의 30 m 버퍼에 속하는 셀 중심으로 계산한다.
궤적 샘플 간격은 해상도/2 이하이고 버퍼 경계의 최대 오차는 해상도/4이다.

`verify_maps.py`는 PGM/YAML, Nav2 셀 의미, 좌표/크기, 원본 및 정렬 SHA256,
PCD crop/ENU 좌표, 주행 영역 통계, 그림 크기와 비어 있지 않음을 검증한다.
실제 Nav2 노드 기동 대신 trinary 분류식을 검증한다.

위 pytest 명령에서 제외한 기존 테스트 1개는 rev1에서 제거한 보조 YAML을 요구한다.
수정 허용 범위 밖인 `tools/tests/`는 유지하며, `tools/maps/test_revision.py`에
단일 YAML의 새 요구사항을 검증하는 테스트를 두었다. 상세 결과와 원래 테스트의
실패 기록은 `results/maps/logs/task06.md`에 있다. 해당 로그는 사용자의 경로
제한에 따라 `logs/task06.md` 대신 작성했다.
